      527.46,
      271.84
    ],
    "text": "has been over ruled in SC Appeal No. 123/09- SC SPL. LA Application 139/09 ~~ minute dated 18.01.2012. According to the Judgment in the case of Muniandy the Supreme Court held inter alia that the provisions containing in Section 28A (3) of the UDA Act fall within the scope of the term \"planning\" and therefore the powers, duties and functions referred to therein could be delegated by the UDA to any officer of the Local Authority and therefore the objection raised by the Respondent-Petitioner-Respondent should fail.",
